IMPORT prelude

-- Section 3: Definitions, "In this Act—".
-- Each definition is a function of the facts that the definition names.
-- A term that the text hands to another Act ("has the same meaning as in ...") is asked as a fact: the other Act is not among the sources.
-- The two defined terms that sections 4 and 5 introduce themselves ("fee unit", "annual rate") are encoded where they appear.

§ `Section 3 -- Definitions`

-- "includes" opens the list: a charge or another amount is a fee, and the text does not say what else is.
-- So a thing that is none of the three has no answer here.
-- src:42 | fee includes charge or other amount;
@ref s 3 fee (src:42)
GIVEN `the item is a fee in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is an other amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- the item is a fee` MEANS
    IF     `the item is a fee in the ordinary sense`
        OR `the item is a charge`
        OR `the item is an other amount`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:44 | instrument maker has the same meaning as in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994;
@ref s 3 instrument maker (src:44)
GIVEN `the person is an instrument maker as the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 uses the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- the person is an instrument maker` MEANS
    `the person is an instrument maker as the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 uses the term`

-- src:46 | legislative instrument has the same meaning as in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994;
@ref s 3 legislative instrument (src:46)
GIVEN `the instrument is a legislative instrument as the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 uses the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- the instrument is a legislative instrument` MEANS
    `the instrument is a legislative instrument as the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 uses the term`

-- "means a fine or other monetary penalty and includes an amount payable ... in respect of an offence for which an infringement notice can be issued".
-- "means" closes the definition at its two limbs, so a thing outside both answers JUST FALSE.
-- The 'includes' limb needs three facts together: payable under an Act or statutory rule, in respect of an offence, and an infringement notice can be issued under the Act.
-- src:47 | penalty means a fine or other monetary penalty and includes an amount payable under an Act or statutory rule in respect of an offence for which an infringement notice can be issued under the Act;
@ref s 3 penalty (src:47)
GIVEN `the item is a fine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is another monetary penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is an amount payable under an Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is payable in respect of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an infringement notice can be issued for that offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- the item is a penalty` MEANS
    JUST (`a fine or other monetary penalty` OR `an amount of the kind the definition includes`)
    WHERE
        `a fine or other monetary penalty` MEANS
                `the item is a fine`
            OR  `the item is another monetary penalty`
        `an amount of the kind the definition includes` MEANS
                `the item is an amount payable under an Act or statutory rule`
            AND `it is payable in respect of an offence`
            AND `an infringement notice can be issued for that offence under the Act`

-- src:48 | penalty unit has the same meaning as in section 110 of the Sentencing Act 1991;
@ref s 3 penalty unit (src:48)
GIVEN `the thing is a penalty unit within the meaning of section 110 of the Sentencing Act 1991` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- the thing is a penalty unit` MEANS
    `the thing is a penalty unit within the meaning of section 110 of the Sentencing Act 1991`

-- src:49 | statutory rule has the same meaning as in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994.
@ref s 3 statutory rule (src:49)
GIVEN `the instrument is a statutory rule as the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 uses the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- the instrument is a statutory rule` MEANS
    `the instrument is a statutory rule as the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 uses the term`
